From 4ca2e88410ddd173ed24ce563d69f0dcdd2bb35e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 05:06:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] fix(gateway): answer every gateway error with the JSON
 envelope

The rate limiter's 429, the 502 when the reverse proxy or the stream
proxy gets no response from the control plane or an instance, and
net/http's default 404 for paths no route matches were plain text,
without a code, a correlation id or a trace id, unlike the gateway's
other errors. Clients had to special-case them, and the response
could not be matched to the logs by its body.

They now use the shared envelope with stable codes: RATE_LIMITED
(Retry-After is unchanged), UPSTREAM_UNAVAILABLE, INVALID_UPSTREAM
when the request to an instance cannot be built, and ROUTE_NOT_FOUND
for unknown paths. Under /api/v1/ the 404 still goes through the
whole chain; elsewhere it gets the correlation id, the trace id and an
access log line but, as before, no authentication or rate limit.
/metrics answers methods other than GET and HEAD with
METHOD_NOT_ALLOWED. Status codes and existing codes are unchanged,
and responses from the control plane or instances pass through
untouched.

Unknown paths do not reuse the control plane's NOT_FOUND because the
CLI reads that code as "the resource does not exist": with it, a
wrong --api-url would make "forgemesh wait --for delete" succeed at
once. The CLI still picks its exit code from the status, so the
envelopes change only its messages. A 404 with any other code still
exits 1 and, as for the plain-text 404 before, tells the user to check
--api-url. Plain-text 429 and 502 can now only come from something in
front of the gateway, so the CLI no longer attributes them to it.
